**Reason both were skipped:** The vulnerable code path in `vaapi_hevc_start_frame()` is only reachable via `-hwaccel vaapi`, which requires:
1. A VAAPI-capable GPU with a working `libva` driver (vainfo returned no output despite `/dev/dri/renderD128` and `renderD129` being present)
2. FFmpeg built with `--enable-vaapi` (the binary at `build_test/ffmpeg` does not list `vaapi` in its `-hwaccels` output)

Neither condition is met on this system, so the vulnerable code is unreachable via any crafted media file passed to the available binary. Status files and notes are written to `/data/ylwang/non-textfuzz/target/_poc/FFmpeg/libavcodec_vaapi_hevc_c/`.
